3. ESP32 firmware for the chip emulator (experimental; LGPL-2.1-or-later)

   When asked for the emulator engine, the compile server builds a student's
   sketch into real ESP32 firmware. Each image is a combined work of:

   - the sketch;
   - Espressif's Arduino core for the ESP32, release 3.3.12, Copyright
     Espressif Systems and contributors, LGPL-2.1-or-later. Its complete
     corresponding source, unmodified, is in third_party/arduino-esp32/, with
     how to rebuild or relink the firmware in its README;
   - Espressif's ESP-IDF 5.5.5 libraries, Apache-2.0, with parts under other
     permissive licences listed in Espressif's own copyright notice
     (https://docs.espressif.com/projects/esp-idf/en/v5.5.5/esp32/COPYRIGHT.html).

   No such firmware is shipped with the application yet.

   The emulator itself, esp32sim (MIT, Copyright its authors), is built from
   its source by third_party/esp32sim/build.sh, and boots Espressif's mask ROM
   for the ESP32 (Apache-2.0).

